 # redb - Changelog
 
+## Kasumi unintegrated capacity prototype
+* Distinguish ordinary growth-capacity denial from failed admission ownership.
+  Owner failure closes new transactions, commits, and page acquisition for that
+  database; previously issued values and cursor fast paths still require an
+  embedding service's response fences and worker drain.
+* Add a durable admitted subset with prepared header publication and rollback of
+  commit-preparation capacity denial. Reject volatile adoption, non-durable mode,
+  and savepoint restore; admitted commits neither trim nor allocate an epilogue.
+* Prepare durable page reclamation and shrink changes in private allocator candidates;
+  publish them only with the committed roots, including matching quick-repair bitmaps.
+  Full commit-time rollback and database-wide disk admission remain incomplete.
+* Add opt-in transaction growth admission and an explicit rollback outcome for
+  capacity denials encountered before commit. Commit-time and maintenance capacity
+  admission remain incomplete; this is not a production storage-capacity contract.
+
